---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import HelloWorld from '../../components/HelloWorld.astro'
import ProjectPage from '../../components/ProjectPage.astro'
---

<Layout>
  <ProjectPage title="Hello world !">
    <HelloWorld slot="project-code" />

    <Fragment slot="project-description">
      <p>
        Well... we all need to start somewhere, isn't it ? So this first scene
        is a very basic one, that I made after watching the first lessons from
        the course : a full-screen, resizable renderer, a perspective camera,
        some orbit controls set up and a few meshes in a scene.
      </p>
      <p>
        Even though I had already seen a bit of the different geometries
        available in Three.js, I wanted to create an abstract nature visual
        using only BoxGeometries of various size and colors. All the meshes use
        the same material type : MeshBasicMaterial, which allowed me to focus
        only on the colors at first without thinking of the lights.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </ProjectPage>
</Layout>
